---
// English-only guide essay. Not built from the number-page template —
// freeform prose, isolated under src/pages/en/guide/. Safe to delete
// without touching the Korean site or the number pages.
import LayoutEn from "../../../layouts/LayoutEn.astro";

const site = "https://angel-sandy-five.vercel.app";
const title = "How to Find Your Angel Number";
const description =
  "Two different things people mean by 'my angel number' — how to calculate your life path number from your birthdate with a worked example, and how to notice repeating numbers in daily life.";
const url = `${site}/en/guide/how-to-find-your-angel-number`;

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  headline: title,
  description,
  url,
  publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "AngelDone" },
  mainEntityOfPage: { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": url },
};
---

<LayoutEn title={title} description={description} canonical={url}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="text-sm text-angel-muted mb-6 flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
      <a href="/en/" class="hover:text-angel-primary transition-colors">Home</a>
      <span>›</span>
      <a href="/en/guide/" class="hover:text-angel-primary transition-colors">Guides</a>
      <span>›</span>
      <span class="text-angel-text">How to Find Your Angel Number</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-angel-text mb-3">How to Find Your Angel Number</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-angel-accent font-medium mb-10">
      A step-by-step way to calculate your life path number, plus how to notice the numbers already showing up around you
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-angel-muted leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-angel-text mb-3">Two different things people mean by "my angel number"</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          Before calculating anything, it's worth separating two ideas that get used interchangeably
          but aren't the same thing. The first is a <strong class="text-angel-text">life path
          number</strong> — a single, fixed number calculated from your birthdate, similar in spirit
          to a sun sign in astrology. It doesn't change, and it's meant to describe a broad
          personality theme rather than a specific message for right now.
        </p>
        <p>
          The second is a <strong class="text-angel-text">recurring number</strong> — something like
          <a href="/en/number/111" class="text-angel-primary hover:text-angel-accent">111</a> or
          <a href="/en/number/717" class="text-angel-primary hover:text-angel-accent">717</a>
          that you keep noticing in daily life, on clocks, receipts, or license plates. This one
          changes over time and is read as situational, tied to whatever's happening in your life
          right now, rather than a fixed personal trait. Most of the number pages on this site are
          about this second kind. This guide covers how to find both.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-angel-text mb-3">Calculating your life path number</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          The most common method is straightforward: write out your full birthdate as digits, add
          every digit together, and keep reducing the total until you land on a single digit — with
          one exception, covered below. Here's a worked example using a birthdate of
          November 23, 1990 (11/23/1990):
        </p>
        <div class="bg-angel-card border border-angel-border rounded-2xl p-6 mb-3">
          <p class="mb-2"><strong class="text-angel-text">Step 1 — Write out every digit:</strong> 1, 1, 2, 3, 1, 9, 9, 0</p>
          <p class="mb-2"><strong class="text-angel-text">Step 2 — Add them all together:</strong> 1+1+2+3+1+9+9+0 = 26</p>
          <p><strong class="text-angel-text">Step 3 — Reduce to a single digit:</strong> 2+6 = 8</p>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-3">
          For this example birthdate, the life path number is
          <a href="/en/number/8" class="text-angel-primary hover:text-angel-accent">8</a> — you'd
          then read what 8 means on this site the same way you'd read any other number.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-3">
          The one exception: if your total, at any point in the reduction, lands on 11, 22, or 33,
          stop there rather than reducing further. These are treated as master numbers with their
          own distinct meaning (see
          <a href="/en/number/11" class="text-angel-primary hover:text-angel-accent">11</a>,
          <a href="/en/number/22" class="text-angel-primary hover:text-angel-accent">22</a>, and
          <a href="/en/number/33" class="text-angel-primary hover:text-angel-accent">33</a>).
        </p>
        <p class="mb-3">
          Here's what that looks like with a birthdate that actually lands on one: August 29, 2001
          (08/29/2001).
        </p>
        <div class="bg-angel-card border border-angel-border rounded-2xl p-6 mb-3">
          <p class="mb-2"><strong class="text-angel-text">Step 1 — Write out every digit:</strong> 0, 8, 2, 9, 2, 0, 0, 1</p>
          <p><strong class="text-angel-text">Step 2 — Add them all together:</strong> 0+8+2+9+2+0+0+1 = 22</p>
        </div>
        <p>
          The total already lands on 22, a master number, so the calculation stops right there
          instead of continuing on to 2+2=4. For this birthdate, the life path number is
          <a href="/en/number/22" class="text-angel-primary hover:text-angel-accent">22</a>, not 4.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-angel-text mb-3">Noticing repeating numbers in daily life</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          Unlike a life path number, you can't calculate a recurring number in advance — you notice
          it because it keeps showing up. A few things make the pattern easier to spot:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-angel-text">Keep a simple running note.</strong> A note on your
            phone works fine. Each time a number catches your attention, jot down the number, where
            you saw it, and what you were thinking about right before.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-angel-text">Check the usual places.</strong> Clocks, receipts,
            license plates, page numbers, order confirmations, and phone numbers are where most
            people first notice a pattern.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-angel-text">Give it a week or two.</strong> One sighting is a
            coincidence. The same number showing up three or four times over a week or two is worth
            actually looking up.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-angel-text">Look for the context, not just the number.</strong> The
            situation you're in when you notice it (mid-decision, right after a hard conversation)
            is often as informative as the number itself.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-angel-text mb-3">What to do with what you find</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          Once you have a number, whether it's your calculated life path number or something you've
          noticed repeating, look up its specific meaning rather than treating "angel numbers" as
          one broad category — the meanings are genuinely different from one number to the next.
          If the number that keeps showing up seems tied to a specific relationship, our
          <a href="/en/guide/twin-flame-numbers" class="text-angel-primary hover:text-angel-accent">twin flame numbers guide</a>
          covers which numbers carry that association most strongly and why.
        </p>
        <p>
          And if you're new to the whole idea and want the background first, our
          <a href="/en/guide/what-is-an-angel-number" class="text-angel-primary hover:text-angel-accent">what is an angel number</a>
          guide covers where the tradition comes from and how to think about it without taking it
          more literally than it's meant.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex justify-between items-center text-sm flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/en/guide/what-is-an-angel-number" class="text-angel-primary hover:text-angel-accent transition-colors">← What is an angel number?</a>
      <a href="/en/guide/twin-flame-numbers" class="text-angel-primary hover:text-angel-accent transition-colors">Twin flame numbers →</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</LayoutEn>
